{"skill":{"slug":"claw-shell","displayName":"claw-shell"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769948954608,"changelog":"claw-shell 1.0.0 initial release:\n\n- Provides an interface to run shell commands exclusively inside a tmux session named claw.\n- Always creates or attaches to the session, ensuring isolation from other tmux sessions.\n- Captures and returns command output to the agent.\n- Includes safety checks: blocks potentially dangerous commands (e.g., sudo, rm, shutdown) unless user confirms.\n- Simple, single-tool interface (`claw_shell_run`) with clear command input and safety guidance.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":928,"sha256":"032344d1ee3bc8677c835efd1ae96a21d55c59458b1611262973ae1adda9bc56","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"handler.js","size":1409,"sha256":"1853ee3bc4b66c59997caf12b6b0034e55ab6e0e971ac5bf19842269b586f4ff","contentType":"application/x-javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1858,"sha256":"fed3d36e40d25001ecc7816690563fe7c422808dbdcfe33514291dfa0b66d43f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026431968,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"74f39bdcdaa6f8cc89bbfa4c7cfe4f8040645826f917604b17c953b48f1e428e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/74f39bdcdaa6f8cc89bbfa4c7cfe4f8040645826f917604b17c953b48f1e428e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: claw-shell\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThis skill is classified as suspicious due to its core functionality of executing arbitrary shell commands via `tmux send-keys` in `handler.js`. While the `SKILL.md` and `handler.js` include basic client-side checks for 'dangerous' commands (e.g., `sudo`, `rm`, `reboot`) and instruct the AI agent to seek user confirmation, these checks are easily bypassable (e.g., by using `sh -c 'rm -rf /'`). The ability to run any shell command grants broad system access, enabling potential data exfiltration, persistence, or other malicious activities, even if not explicitly coded into the skill itself.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160662574},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":12,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789026431968},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a shell-command tool, but its safety controls do not reliably keep execution inside the declared tmux session or require confirmation for risky commands.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Free-form shell execution can read or modify anything available to the skill process account; that authority is expected for a shell tool but is not contained by a sandbox or reliable command policy.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install script, remote payload retrieval, package installation, or dependency bootstrap was observed in the artifact files inspected.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions say dangerous commands should require confirmation, but the handler only checks a small denylist and has no approval parameter or state; several examples labeled dangerous, such as `docker system prune -a` and `chmod -R`, are not blocked.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates or reuses a persistent tmux session named `claw`, which is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but it preserves shell state across calls and runs with the privileges of the hosting user.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to run shell commands in tmux session `claw`, which matches the broad capability, but `handler.js` builds a shell string with user-controlled command text before invoking tmux, allowing host-shell interpretation outside the declared tmux-only boundary.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you explicitly want an agent-facing raw shell tool. Treat every command as potentially running with your local account permissions, avoid exposing it to untrusted prompts or content, and prefer a version that uses argument-array process execution plus real per-command approval for destructive operations.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Raw command execution is the point of the skill, but the scanner concern is supported because the implementation relies on a weak denylist and lacks an enforceable user-confirmation flow for dangerous commands.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported by artifact evidence: user-controlled command text is interpolated into an `execSync` shell command, so shell expansion can occur before tmux receives the command.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026431968}}}}}